    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d233-a1">

                <pb facs="0354" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg266"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr.
                            Roman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo
                                City, D. R.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-01-20"><hi rendition="#italic">January 20,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform your excellency
                    that the Government of the United States of North America, through its
                    representative accredited to this Republic, recognizes the Government, of which
                    Gen. Carlos F. Morales is the provisional president, and in view that the said
                    Government is in possession <pb facs="0355" n="267" xml:id="pg267"/> of the
                    capital of the Republic, the archives, the great seal of state, the arsenals,
                    and the principal ports of the Dominican Republic, as being the de facto
                    government of the Republic.</p>
                <p>Allow me, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
